; The customer's DNS, as the CA sees it. example.com is reserved by RFC 2606,
; so serving it here cannot collide with anything real.
;
; THIS IS A TEMPLATE. development/scripts/lib.sh renders it to
; example.com.zone — which is gitignored — substituting the challenge
; delegation below. Edit this file; never the generated one, which the next
; seed overwrites.
;
; The contents mirror what development/scripts/seed.sh puts in the inventory:
; project `demo`, load balancer `prod`, domains `demo.example.com` and
; `*.demo.example.com`. Change the seed and this file must change with it —
; `acmeservice adminctl loadbalancer dns demo/prod` prints exactly what belongs here.
$ORIGIN example.com.
$TTL 60

@   IN SOA ns.example.com. hostmaster.example.com. (
        2026082001 ; serial
        7200       ; refresh
        3600       ; retry
        1209600    ; expire
        60 )       ; minimum
@   IN NS  ns.example.com.
ns  IN A   172.28.0.53

; The customer-like load balancer (traefik-lb) answers for both names. The
; wildcard is what makes `*.demo.example.com` resolve to the same place.
;
; These deliberately DIFFER from the addresses the generated plan prints
; (203.0.113.10/.11, the seeded node addresses — TEST-NET-3, unroutable by
; design). Only the _acme-challenge CNAME below has to match the plan; the A
; records just have to point at something that answers, which here is the
; container.
demo    IN A 172.28.0.30
*.demo  IN A 172.28.0.30

; The one record the whole design turns on. `demo.example.com` and
; `*.demo.example.com` are two domain rows sharing ONE challenge name, hence
; ONE alias, hence ONE CNAME — a certificate covering both validates two
; authorizations at this single name.
;
; The target label is NOT written here and cannot be: with the shipped default
; (ACME_ALIAS_USE_DOMAIN unset) the service generates a random label such as
; jxet64y6bngq4j37, and only the running system knows which one it picked.
; development/scripts/seed.sh reads it back out of
; `adminctl loadbalancer dns demo/prod` and substitutes the CNAME records —
; one per alias — for the marker below.
@@CHALLENGE_DELEGATION@@
